/-
Formal results for the m = 25 pilot (CARD.md, proposal.md): five of the seventeen rules have
every eigenvalue a cube at m = 25, i.e. their period on the 25 x 25 torus divides
341 = (2^10 - 1)/3.

* Cube certificates (mechanism B of proposal.md).  For the square family rules 3096
  (orbits (2,0), (2,1), (4,0), (4,1)) and 23608 ((2,0), (2,1), (2,2), (4,0), (4,1), (4,2), (4,4)),

      f * (t(x) t(y))^3 = B,      t(z) = z + 1/z,       (over GF(2), exactly)

  with B a union of shells permuted by (x, y) -> (x^7, y^7) on the 25-torus (7 = 2^5 mod 25), so
  B's values are fixed by the 2^5-th power: B = 0 or B^31 = 1.  Rule-90 values t satisfy
  t^1024 = t (as z^1024 = 1/z when z^25 = 1), so off the axes f = B / (t(x) t(y))^3 and
  f^341 = B^341 / (t(x) t(y))^1023 = 1.  On the axes f = t^2 (t + 1)^2 = t(z) t(z^3) = t^129.
  `period_r3096_dvd`, `period_r23608_dvd`.

* Twisted pairs (mechanism A).  1227 = C(x, y) C(x^3, y^3) with C = self + N4, 21029 with
  C = self + D4, 32184 with C = N4 + D4.  As 3 = 2^7 mod 25, C(x^3, y^3) = C(x, y)^128 on the
  torus, so the eigenvalue is c^129 = (c^3)^43 with c^1023 = 1 (c^1024 = C(1/x, 1/y) = c).
  `period_r1227_dvd`, `period_r21029_dvd`, `period_r32184_dvd`.

The polynomial identities are checked by `linear_combination` (certificates generated by
scratch/genlean.py); everything else is proved here.
-/
